WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.510
Home! Home?

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.010
Home!

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.020
Home? Home!

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.020
Could be around any corner.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.020
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.020
♪ Chop the wood to light the fire ♪

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.020
Hey, captain, do you hear that singing?

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.010
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.190
Graawr

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.520
Not you, skipper.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.110
I'm talking to the captain.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.450
♪ Tis it much that I require! ♪

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.120
Captain Wirt, do
you know who's singing?

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:00.370
I don't know much
of anything anymore.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.560
♪ When the fog of life surrounds you, ♪

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:01.570
Oh.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.810
Did you know that dinosaurs had big ears,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.370
♪ when you feel you've lost your way! ♪

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.040
but everyone forgot 'cause dinosaur ears don't have bones?

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.410
♪ Come with me and join the forest, ♪

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.540
No. I... I didn't know that, Greg.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.300
♪ Come with me and join the play! ♪

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.350
That's 'cause it's not true.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.300
It's a rock fact!

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.850
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.760
The beast.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.970
It must be the beast out there.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.960
♪ Youth is such a fragile thing. ♪

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.740
The obsidian cricket of our inevitable twilight

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.860
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.140
singing our requiem.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.590
♪ A fragile thing is what it is. ♪

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.140
Hmm. Yeah!

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.680
Must be a really fat cricket.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.150
Look! We've reached land!

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.150
Feel the dirt!

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.150
Ahh. Smell that tree.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:36.150
We must be almost there.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.410
Greg?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.320
Yes, Wirt?

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.410
Can we please stop pretending we're gonna get home?

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.080
Huh?

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.080
Can we admit we're lost for good?

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.830
This fog is deeper than we can ever understand?

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.460
We are but wayward leaves,

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.920
scattered to the air
by an indifferent wind?

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.380
Can we just admit we're never gonna get back home, Greg?

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.340
Can we do that?

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.610
Wirt, you can do anything if you set your mind to it.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.340
That's what the old people say.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.010
Well, then let's do that.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.010
Yes, sir, captain!

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.000
Greg!

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.850
You need to stop acting ridiculous all the time.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.440
Huh?

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.440
Look, do you even know why we got lost in the first place?

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.810
It's 'cause you were goofing around

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.610
and getting into trouble like you always do.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.200
Really? It was all my fault?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.840
Yeah, so...

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.940
it's not my job to get us home, okay?

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.950
I'm done.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.370
Are you saying I should be the leader?

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.200
I don't care what you do.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.560
But if I'm the leader...

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.710
what are you gonna be?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.040
I'll be asleep.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.850
Wow. Well...

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.800
then I better take a nap, too.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.800
I need to dream up a good way of leading us home.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.050
Thanks for trusting me, Wirt.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.010
Don't worry.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.260
I won't let you down.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.260
I'll be a good leader.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.060
Good night.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.780
Star, oh, star, up in the sky,

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.150
guide my dreams with light that shines.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.320
Help me know just what to do

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.710
to get Wirt home and also me, too.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.740
And if you don't, I don't care.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.910
I'll pull down your underwear.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.140
♪ Forward, cherubs ♪

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.920
♪ hear the song ♪

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.920
♪ a child's wishes ♪

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.100
♪ call us on ♪

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:30.270
♪ Descend! Descend! ♪

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.100
Psst! Hey!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.770
Huh? Whoa!

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:38.780
♪ The dreams our winged ♪

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:44.530
♪ wind hath made ♪

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:51.060
♪ for only beneath ♪

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.700
♪ the veil ♪

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.700
Whoa.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.340
♪ Of sleep ♪

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.080
WhooOooa!

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:01.920
Whoa!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.130
Whooooaa!

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.470
Wow!

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:08.970
Hey, Greg!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:09.970
- Hello!
- Welcome!

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.650
- Nice to see you!
- Hello!

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:12.870
Come on in!

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:14.230
Hey, everybody!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.980
Welcome to Cloud City!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.650
Thank you! Thank you!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.820
My name's Greg.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:19.900
What are yours?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.900
♪ We're the Cloud City ♪

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.900
♪ Reception Commitee! ♪

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.240
♪ And we are here to welcome thee ♪

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.160
Oh, wow, neat.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.160
♪ And we're the Cloud City ♪

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.980
♪ Auxiliary Reception Committee ♪

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:41.010
♪ and we are also here
to welcome thee ♪

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.020
Thank you.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.680
♪ And we're the hippopotamus,
giraffe, and monkey ♪

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.180
♪ and we are committee no. 3 ♪

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.100
Okay. Are there more?

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.380
Well, that's enough.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.780
So, what brings you to Cloud City?

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.910
Well, I'm supposed to be a leader,

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.300
but I don't know how.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.950
Why don't you lead our band in a song?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:08.570
Okay.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:20.750
♪ Everything is nice
and fine all the time ♪

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.760
♪ the softest clouds and rainbow skies ♪

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.590
♪ ain't gonna lie ♪

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:30.600
♪ we always have the most
spectacular time together ♪

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:35.940
♪ everyone is sittin' pretty
on top of the weather ♪

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.360
♪ lasso a cloud and
make the flowers grow ♪

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.530
♪ tie them in a bow to throw
at the end of the show ♪

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:50.530
♪ our songs are filled with love ♪
♪ the sweetest love ♪

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:55.490
♪ and we can send them down to you ♪
♪ with a little shove ♪

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:02.880
♪ so hitch a ride into the sky ♪
♪ and join our band ♪

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.630
♪ bring harps and lutes, kazoos,
trombones and flutes ♪

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.640
♪ or just your pots and pans ♪

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.710
♪ we can write a little jig
out of the mighty blue ♪

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.060
♪ and we will be here just for you- ♪

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.200
Hehe...

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:26.820
Bonk.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.240
Oh, nooooo!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.240
The North wind is loose!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.410
♪ Oh, yeah, the ol' North wind ♪

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.340
♪ starts to howl ♪

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.540
♪ puffs up and furrows his brow ♪

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.810
♪ now, now ♪

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.600
♪ you better take cover ♪

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.340
♪ lock up those doors ♪

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.350
♪ and close the shutters ♪

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.320
♪ I say, the ol' North wind ♪

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.060
♪ yes, he is ♪

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.460
♪ he's gonna fight ♪
♪ he's gonna spin ♪

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:05.520
♪ he's gonna pull back ♪
♪ and blow a little more ♪

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.610
♪ until you can't tell
what you came here for ♪

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.700
♪ oh, yeah The ol' North wind♪

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.280
Fire!

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:17.500
♪ Yes, indeed ♪
♪ he's gonna breathe and breathe ♪

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.000
♪ he's gonna blow ♪

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.820
♪ blow till you can't feel no more ♪

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.050
Wirt? Greg?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.680
Is anyone out there?

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.050
Ah!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.490
Hey, North wind!

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.660
Pbht!

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.400
Errh, I don't like that one bit.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.740
That makes me mad!

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.960
Oh, no!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.060
Hee hee hee hee!

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.230
Huh?

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.690
Why, hello, Gregory.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.690
Hello.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.310
I am the Queen of the Clouds.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.820
Thank you for saving my city.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:35.820
You're welcome.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.830
I shall grant you one wish.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.490
What do you wish for most of all?

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:45.160
Well, I'm supposed to be the leader, but I don't know how to get home.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:45.880
Do you know?

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.960
Of course.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.840
If you wish, I can gcertainly send you home.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.840
Great! Let's go get Wirt.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.330
I'm sorry, Gregory,

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.970
but Wirt cannot go with you.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.510
He is too lost.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.510
Huh!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:58.200
But...

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.970
anything is possible if you set your mind to it, right?

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.980
See how the edelwood grows around him?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.520
The beast has claimed him already.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.800
Oh, I should have
been leading better.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.400
I was goofing off again, like always,

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.530
and now you're stuck here.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.490
Isn't there anything I can do?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.490
I'm sorry, Gregory.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.250
Wirt's fate lies solely in the beast's hands now.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.420
Then I know what to wish for.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.460
Are you sure?

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.960
Then it shall be done.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.580
Hey. Hey, Wirt?

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.010
Shh! I'm trying to sleep!

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.930
Okay. You sleep.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.810
I'm sorry I got us lost, Wirt.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:48.380
Will you take care of Ronald for me?

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.940
Okay. I have to go now.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:52.800
Goodbye, Wirt.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.800
Yes. Come, Gregory.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.950
There is much to be done.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.490
and then you'll show us the way home, right?

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.950
Of course.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.740
We made a promise, didn't we?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.290
Greg. Greg?

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.290
Greg? Greg?!

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.290
Where did he go?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.880
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.730
No. No, no, no, no!

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:11.850
Greg?!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.950
♪ Chop the wood to light the fire ♪

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.960
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:15.300
What the heck?

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:20.130
♪ Tis it much that I require! ♪

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.300
Greg?!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.850
Greg... What did I do?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.100
Greg! Greg!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:29.940
♪ when you feel you've lost your way! ♪

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.940
♪ Come with me and join the forest, ♪

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.940
Huh? Greg!

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.690
♪ Come with me and join the play! ♪

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.490
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.570
Oh! You got him!

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.460
Pull! Pull!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.830
Is he alive?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.460
- Wirt!
- Wirt? Wirt!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.130
Gr...eg...?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.130
Wirt, are you okay?

00:10:58.130 --> 00:10:59.130
Wirt!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.050
Gr...eg? I-I-I...

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.300
Where's Greg, Wirt?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.300
Beatrice?

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:08.060
Wirt? Wirt!

